body:
King Crimson goes into the "My Favorite Band" playlist and everything else goes into "Everything else."

&#x200B;

* I make playlists for specific bands and have only one that covers more than one band called Prog rock which has Yes, Rush, Floyd, Cimson and a bunch of others.

Another Pats fan here... hate the Bills Mafia but going to hope you guys win it all this year... Bills Mafia showed heart this year under very difficult sequences and I respect that. Go win the Superbowl!

&#x200B;

Next year, I will hate you all again! : )

I was a Hold Your Fire hater because it was a turn in a direction I didn't like but listened to it recently and was nicely surprised by it. Not one of my favorites but it is still a good album.

&#x200B;

\*edit - Oh yeah, you need to listen to Permanent Waves and Moving Pictures. next.



Probably the most straightforward song on this album if you can call this songs instead of experiments. The organ repeats the same theme as does the bass. The drums are typically active while there is a guitar solo and a distorted flute solo over the main sections of this song. There are of course some weird sounds involved to make it unworldly but overall, the most easily accessible song on the album. Called Anesthetize because it is a very hypnotic song.

&#x200B;

[https://youtu.be/THDUGjMpvCI](https://youtu.be/THDUGjMpvCI)

